From: RSD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] zynq: reserve upper 256 MiB of ZedBoard DDR for RSD

Keep U-Boot relocation and allocations out of the memory owned by RSD.
The Linux device tree uses the same split.

--- a/arch/arm/dts/zynq-zed.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/zynq-zed.dts
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 
 	memory@0 {
 		device_type = "memory";
-		reg = <0x0 0x20000000>;
+		reg = <0x0 0x10000000>;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
